# Loaded ONLY by `npm run build:firefox` (vite --mode firefox), overriding .env.
#
# dist-firefox/ is never a local daily driver — it is only ever the
# self-host/AMO distribution artifact (REVIEWER-BUILD.md). build-firefox.mjs
# already strips the localhost HOST PERMISSION for exactly that reason, but the
# API URL itself is baked into the JS by vite long before that script runs, so
# stripping the permission was only ever half the guard: a developer .env with
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 silently produced a "distribution"
# build that pointed every request at the builder's own machine. Confirmed live
# on 2026-08-02 — a signed Firefox build POSTing to http://localhost:8000 and
# failing NS_ERROR_CONNECTION_REFUSED.
#
# Committed deliberately (see the !.env.firefox exception in .gitignore): it
# holds no secret, and the whole point is that the distribution build does not
# depend on whatever happens to be in an untracked .env.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://retainhq.onrender.com
